i think this happens because Digital UNIX uses (like most othere modern unices
too) demand paging of executables - i.e. it reads pages which are unused at
the program start later if it needs them - if you now delete the executable it
will die if it needs a page it doesn't have in memory and wanted to read it
from the executable file which doesn't exit any longer

maybe you can avoid it by using a special linker option (don't have a man page
of the Digital UNIX linker handy here - run FreeBSD at home :-) or simply
moving it to a new name and delete it later - don't know what you need the
deletability for

