>My questions are, how do I install the new firmware? I followed the
>DEC manual, and typed

Stick the firmware CD in and boot from it at the hardware prompt like this:

>> boot -fl 0,80 dka###

where dka### is the device of your CD drive. Use 'show device' to find out.

If all goes well, you'll be prompted for a bootfile name. The name of the
filw for a 3000/400 is this:

[DEC3000]M400_V###.EXE

where ### is the version number of the firmware you are installing. This
varies from machine to machine. You need to check the release notes that
came with the firmware CD and find the version that's on your CD.

The format of ### above should be in the form of #_#, so if you are trying
to install version 6.1, the above bootfile would be:

[DEC3000]M400_V6_1.EXE

If that works, you'll get a menu which allows you to update the firmware.

Of course, that won't work unless you have the firmware update jumper in the
correct position....

>How many installations do I need to do to get to 3.2C?? Three? 

One full install, lots of update installs. I'd go with a full install.

Good luck.

