David Adamec wrote:
> 
> David M. Carver wrote:
> >
> > I am trying to install Digital's Parallel Software Environment (PSE) on
> > an Alpha running Digital UNIX 3.2c. One of the software subsets required
> > is PSEKBIN300100, which is dependent on OSFBIN300 for installation. On
> > checking which subsets we have installed, I can see that we have
> > OSFBIN350 (Standard Kernel Objects) already installed. However, when I
> > try and install the PSEKBIN300100 subset, setld complains that it
> > *must* have OSFBIN300 installed.

First, let me correct the above statement.  The PSEKBIN300100 subset
is optional, not required.  PSE will work just fine without installing
this subset.  The PSEKBIN300100 subset contains kernel object files
that provide a PSE-specific optimization to the UDP protocol.  Refer
to the PSE manual or the last Digital Technical Journal article 
(http://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/DECinfo/DTJ/v7n3_04_PSE.ps) for
exactly what the optimization does.

Without the PSEKBIN300100 subset, PSE will use the standard UDP
implementation that is in the Digital UNIX kernel.

Unfortunately, PSEKBIN300100 contains kernel object files that might
not be compatible with kernels other than DEC OSF/1 V3.0, hence the
dependency check for OSFBIN300 subset.

The upcoming release of PSE (V1.1) will contain three PSEKBINnnnvvv
subsets, supporting DEC OSF/1 V3.0, V3.2, and Digital UNIX V3.2C.
This release will be available in April '96.

> >
> > Here's my list of questions:
> >
> >         1. Will PSEKBIN300100 work with OSFBIN350?

No.

> >         2. If so, how can I force it to install?

You probably can, but don't.

> >         3. If not, is it safe to install OSFBIN300?

No.

...

> One option that might work is to
> 
>    touch /usr/.smdb/OSFBIN300.lk
> 
> as root. WARNING ---- I haven't tried this, I'm too scared that
> this will royally screw my 2100, but it would be an easier
> solution than installing OSFBIN300 if it works. Anyone have
> any feelings what this touch would do if OSFBIN350 is installed?
> 

This suggestion will force install PSEKBIN300100, but it is not
supported and very dangerous.  I have not tried it myself and won't
even try.  The consequences of doing this is replacing the existing
V3.2C socket, IP, UDP, and the fta driver code with the V3.0 code.

So the bottom line is to not install PSEKBIN300100, and if you need
it, PSEKBIN350110 will be available soon.  Let me know if you have
any further questions.

