When it comes to results for a specific piece of code, there is no way
to say for sure which complier will yield the best results. I don't find
either gcc or cc to be especially stellar. cc-migrate used the MIPS
developed GEM technology which is claimed to be excellent. (I have done
no actual tests, so I will not vouch for the validity of the claims.)
 
