>> UBC write error(70) on device (0, 0) at block 0 size 8192

These messages are often associated with NFS mounted file system.  Especially
when the device number is 0 (major 0, minor 0).  The error(#) number is the
errno value corresponding to the error, which happens to be ESTALE.  I'd
dismount the file system (on the complaining client) and re-mount it.\

