>Alpha/Linux system, 

Probably more, if you want to match the performance of the system you
used to run the "benchmark".  Besides monitor and (at least) another 16
MB RAM, you'll have to add 3.5 MB of cache and an OSF/1 licence (you
want to run X on the Alpha and NT doesn't come with an X server that
can run under Linux, or at all).

>but the P6-180 costs $~4500 and doesn't come with
>SCSI (<$100) or Ethernet ($150 for fast).

The Polywell Alpha doesn't come with Ethernet, either.

