One of the "rules of thumb" I've always followed is:
keep slow devices together/fast devices together.

So I would go with "b". it's not the speed of the tape that should be a =

concern; it's what the tape does to the overall throughput of the =

channel while it is running.

The speed you're looking for is probably better sought after by =

balancing the products between spindles.  If you can group =

users/apps/data so that each has its own spindle, that will give you =

your maximum performance.

