Subject: INFO: DEC 3000 serial port limits
Date: 1996/02/22
Message-ID: <4giaka$9j@news.asu.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 140574117
distribution: world
organization: Dept. of Physics & Astronomy, Arizona State University
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

For those of you who have a DEC 3000 300/400/600 unit and don't know 
this, here's the main poop.  The serial line ports will not support
any speed greater than 9600 baud.  This is an acknowledged design flaw
in those units by DEC, but doesn't help those of us saddled with those
machines who need to communicate through the interface at faster speeds.

We have filed a software call on this matter with DEC since a hardware 
specialist at DEC seems convinced that the problem is not a hardware 
related issue - ie. the interface can talk at faster than 9600 baud, 
but the software (ie. the firmware) has never been written to include 
higher speeds in the serial line handling.  This may also be a kernel 
configuration issue.

As and when we hear some resolution to this matter I'll post an update.

