>other pointers that might help me along while I am learning? 
>Thanks alot.

If you want to install a pop daemon on OSF/1, perhaps i may help you

You can have more informations with man pop,popd and popaka

1) Create a user named pop
2) In his home directory, create a file named POP (see man pop for
more details)
3) In /var/adm/sendmail/sendmail.cf, verify there is a rule which
redirect pop mail requests
4) with /usr/lib/mh/popaka, insert "pop" users in mail aliases file
5) launch /usr/lib/mh/popd with a correct port number (110 for pop3)

Well, i think that's all








