Hi..

I have had the same problem with a HP1600 CM color network printer.
The printers "Auto Detect" function could make the choice between
PCL or PostScript if exist the following line for the device 
in the /etc/printcap file:  rp:raw:\

But if you send a normal textfile, the printer can't detect the
end-of-line and can't form the document. The solution is the
following line in the printcap file: rp:text:\
(ps. I don't know if this works for Lexmark.)

So if you don't have a program to form a textfile to postscript
you have to make two printer definitions, one for text and one
for "raw". If your printer accept postscript only you need to
form the document. I don't know if Digital UNIX have this 
capability. It could be usefull me too!

Regards
Zoltan




