: : Is this right?  Are there any rules for the numbering scheme of files in
: : /sbin/rc3.d?

The numbering system is such that globbing controls the execution order -
I assume you are aware of this ? (S00XXX will precede S01XXX etc).
Your numeric portion has to be 2 digits (S100XX is bad). Remember how globbing 
works.

: I don't think there are any rules for that. Just choose a unuses number.

It's probably good practice to start any local init.d scripts after the
vendor one's have run, especially if you have other services that you
expect to be running.

On my system for example, I'd start local stuff at S85 (S80/crashdc is the
last vendor script to be started)


