In article <31285C71.2781@zuo.dec.com>, 
Arnold Sutter <noldi@zuo.dec.com> writes...
>Nick Potkay wrote:
>> Sometime ago we bought a couple of alpha axp 200's, they came loaded with
>> srm firmware.  From that we installed DGUX.  But now, we need to install
>> NT. I know in order to install NT we need to load the arc firmware.  Any
>> one know how to load the arc firmware from cd?  Any help would be
>> appreciated.
>> 
>You ALREADY have the ARC console loaded. Typing 'arc' at the console prompt 
>should bring you into the ARC FW. 
> 

     Early versions of the AlphaStation shipped with both the ARC (used for
     Windows NT) and SRM (used for Digital UNIX and OpenVMS) consoles. 
     Later units have only one console installed, but you can load the
     other from the firmware CD.

     -- Kenny


     To load ARC ...

     Powerup system and get it to the SRM console prompt (>>>)

     >>> b -fl 0,A0 dka600
     BOOTFILE:[alpha200]as200_v5_0.exe	! located on the 3.3 firmware cd

     Apu-> update ARC
     	APU-I *** ROMS 0,1 CONTENTS WILL BE DESTROYED ***
     	APU-I ARE YOU READY TO PROGRAM DEVICE ? (Y/N ) y
     Apu-> verify
     	ARC Rom Verify Successful
     Apu-> quit
     					! powerfail system to change from 
     					! SRM to ARC boot window


     To load SRM ...

     Powerup system, go to WNT boot menu

     Go to the Supplementary menu
     This menu selection is the last choice in the Boot Menu.

     Go to the Install New Firmware selection
     When selected the CDROM will be checked for the firmware
     update utility latest version and bring it up to the Apu-> prompt

     Apu-> update SRM
     	APU-I *** ROMS 0,1 CONTENTS WILL BE DESTROYED ***
     	APU-I ARE YOU READY TO PROGRAM DEVICE ? (Y/N ) y
     Apu-> verify
     	SRM Rom Verify Successful
     Apu-> quit

     powerfail system to change from ARC to SRM boot window

