>
> the setting i know is (from our other machines resp. displays):
>   default number of colormap cells:    256
>   preallocated pixels:    black 1, white 0
> 
> i have no idea if this is the reason ... and i dont know how one could
> change it
> to try it.
> 
> rupert.
> 
> ps:
> do you also get warnings when starting up netscape?

Use netscape -install to run netscape. This tells netscape to install
its own colormap, so you don't trash the default colormap, and trash the
visuals on other windows. It seems to behave much better this way.

Yes, 2.0 is *statically* linked to X11R5, due to some
internationalization issue, so warnings like "C locale not found" pop up
when running. You need the now defunct directory /usr/lib/X11/nls
containing a whole bunch of wacky I18N type files. This also solves the
cut/paste crash. It should have been in the netscape distribution you
received.

It is also recommended to set (in your $HOME/.Xdefaults file) the
resource:
Netscape*maxImageColors:        96
This makes netscape use a maximum of 96 colors. Useful if you don't want
netscape to install its own colormap. With this resource set, the other
windows on the system are able to alloc their colors properly, and
everything behaves.



