Hi,

I got pop mail working on Digital UNIX V3.2C

I tried this with Microsoft Exchange and Eudora clients, and it works a 
treat.

First, do a man of popd.

You need to start a POP3 server with a line something like this (This is 
from memory, and may be wrong!)

# popd -p 110 &

I think it is port 110 for POP3. The manual pages will confirm this.

You also need to add popusers (manual pages describe how!), use popwrd to 
set the password for each pop user, and make sure your sendmail stuff 
already works. Then you need to get your aliases right. This is also in 
the manual pages.

Sorry I don't have more details, but it is reasonably easy once you look 
at the manual pages!

