 > Bad pack magic number (label is damaged, or pack is unlabeled)

I've gotten this message, too.  My workaround is to specify UNKNOWN as
the disk type when writing a new label.  Disklabel then reads disk
parameters from the driver and uses them.  As far as I know, this is
undocumented.  I lucked out in discovering it through playing around
with disklabel.

Example:  disklabel -w rz1 UNKNOWN

If you relabel the disk using this method, you will most likely lose
any existing data, so you might want to use tar to read as musch data
as possible off of the drive.


Good luck!

