, but as I recall, the sequence is:
disklabel -z /dev/rz0c
disklabel -e /dev/rz0c
The last command lets you edit the disk label. You may need to do a
disklabel -wr /dev/rz0c rzxx
before you can do the edit.
When you do the disklabel -e, you can edit the partition table and
change the rotational speed, then write the label. Then, do your
newfs on each partition. You should always do an fsck after you do
your newfs. Good Luck.


