> 
> 	I have a network printer, a dec printserver 17.  It has an ethernet
> address.  I have made several attempts at getting my node to recognize the 
> network printer.  This I have done by trial and error with the printcap file.
> 
> 	Unfortunately, I wasn't able to get the OSF software to spool the 
> files to the network printer.  Can someone give me some hints about network
> printer installation?   (The printer is not attached to a computer.)

Jeff,

You will probably need to load the LPS Printserver software.  I believe it's
on the base DEC OSF sw distribution cdrom.  The LPS software includes a
large number of support files you will need for proper operation of the
Printserver and also installs an LPS specific setup script (/etc/lpssetup)
that you use to configure Printserver queues.

On the printer end, you will somehow need to establish a console session
to the Printserver and configure it with an IP address that is reachable
by the OSF box.  (Un?)Fortunately, I haven't had to do that with our
Printservers as they were already configured for VMS hosts so I was able
to use the VMS console utility to connect to the printer to enable IP.

Hope this helps and good luck.

Henry Maine







