I should have pointed out here that if you use perl5 with majordomo, you
will need to fix a couple of majordomo's scripts which use un-escaped @'s
in "print <<EOF;" blocks.  It's all detailed in the FAQ.

Example:

print <<EOF;
Send mail to fred@foo.bar
EOF

... would work in perl4, but needs to be ...

perint <<EOF;
Sendmail to fred\@foo.bar
EOF

