Two things to check.  Make sure ftp is in your /etc/services file.  It should 
look like something like this ---   ftp        21/tcp .  Make sure there is no
pound sign (#) in front of it.  That will make it a comment.  Also check to see
if you have an /etc/ftpusers file.  If you do and the people trying to ftp into
your OSF host are in that file they will not be allowed.  Simply vi the file
and
remove their name.  It does seem kind of backwards, if you want to ftp DO NOT
put the user in the /etc/ftpusers file and if you don't want them to ftp ADD
them to the /etc/ftpusers file.

Hope this helps,

Bill Reid




