>When looking at two different installation programs supplied via CDROM, 
>I noticed the files were in this format:  filename.;1
>The documentation says to just enter the filename to run the setup.  
>Unfortunately, that doesn't work.  Is the .;1 a standard used for 
>installations, or did I just end up with my first two installations in 
>this format?  

To get rid of the ;1, mount the cdrom like this:

mount -rt cdfs -o noversion /dev/rzxc /cdrom

The semicolon is a special character in shell programming. To run the command, 
enter

filename.\;1

Good Luck.

