They're the slowest Alpha (21064) systems DEC ever built.  Most of the
other answers can be found in the Hardware Reference Guide which comes
with every system.

The 300L has no TURBOchannel slots, so the SCSI bus is the only way to
expand it, the 300LX has two TURBOchannel slots.  Both have 8 72-"pin"
SIMM sockets, which can accept 8 or 32 (or 64?) MB SIMMs.

