Well, that's a very sweeping statement.  My Alpha at home has only 40Mb
and acts as a secondary DNS and our anonymous ftp server (it's on a cable
modem).  If you connect to ftp.garply.com, you'll be talking to it.  I'll 
be running CDE and two copies of Netscape on it as well. 

However, I'm not going to argue that 32Mb is right on the cusp.  I wasn't 
spec'ing a "real" server, just what we put together as a first 
prototype.  I didn't want to order thousands of dollars worth of parity 
RAM and find out that the card wouldn't do what I wanted.

That's the great thing about memory - you just whip out your cheque book, 
and hey presto, you've got more.

