building a communications gateway that will translate between older NASA-custom  
protocols and TCP/IP (and UDP/IP) protocols.  The new system will have some of  
the characteristics of a web server, in that there will be a large volume of  
short duration TCP/IP connections.  We are hoping to rapidly decide on a  
workstation/server platform for the gateway, and need to resolve the following  
situation:
1. We need to support multiple IP addresses on the gateway machine.  We will  
have to support up to 255 virtual domains simultaneously.
2. We would really like to make use of a "high availability" environment that  
will handle failovers at a system level (rather than having to incorporate  
failovers into the applications' logic).  The gateway applications will need  
very little disk space.  Shared disks on the gateway machines will not be  
required; if the high availability environment can function without shared  
disks, we might be able to save some money...
3. The high availability environment must be able to fail over all of the  
virtual domain addresses.

Any suggestions will be greatly appreciated.  ThanxInAdvance...

