Asides:
What DEC should have done is take vxfs at the same time they took the rest of 
Veritas. Putting the reliability issues aside, it would be nice to be able to 
enlarge a block device (volume) and have the filesystem layer see the change. 
The end result of trying to protect the ADVFS development costs is that ADVFS 
and LSM operate fundamentally at odds.

