My favorite (on comp.sys.dec I think) was "LVM is the son of Satan" a comment
on the withdrawal of LVM and it's replacement by LSM.

My best recollection is that the AIX volume manager is based directly off
LVM (which everyone got from the OSF). It was enhanced by IBM - without giving
up and buying a 3rd party solution - works well and is especially well 
integrated with the JFS filesystem layer.
[having said this, it's the only part of AIX that I like :-)].

