I know you all in the Ladebug development group frequent this newsgroup
and care about what we, the users, think of your product -- so I have
some suggestions/things I miss in Ladebug.

We're using Digital UNIX V3.2 Rev. 214, with DECladebug Debugger Version
4.0-8 (command line version).

1)  The $curline and $cursrcline variables seem to be switched
(according to the documentation).
       $curline
            Specifies the current line in the source file.
       $cursrcline
            Specifies the line number of the last line of source code
            listed plus one.
'list' causes $curline to be changed.  This is also inconsistent with
dbx under Digital UNIX.  (the 'w' alias has become one of my favorite
commands since I discovered it in DUNIX's dbx -- no matter what you've
been doing, it will show you the context of your current line.  In
Ladebug, however, 'w' followed by 'list' will mess this up.  I realize
that redefining the alias to use $cursrcline will fix this, but this is
then inconsistent with dbx).

2)  The 'edit' command doesn't exist in Ladebug.  (used to edit the
current source file)  This is one I use a lot in dbx.

3)  Ability to page long output.  (dbx does this by default)  Not as
important using an xterm, but important to me when dialed in from home.

4)  With taso applications (which ours is at this point), I cannot
dereference a pointer as an array.
For example, argv is defined as 'char *argv[]'.  'p argv[0]' returns:
Error: coercion size mismatch
Evaluating 'argv[0]' failed!
The value (0x11fffae8) does not have an element index '0'!
Error: no value for argv[0]

Hope this helps you improve on your product.

Tim
