I am looking at my October 1993 copy of the Digital Systems and Options
Catalog.   Starting on page 1.15 is the description of the DEC 3000 Model
300/300L AXP Desktop Workstations.   On page 1.19 is Step 5, "TURBOchannel
Graphics Upgrades (Model 300 only).   It lists Order Number PMAGB-DA as a
*Factory* *Installed* PXG+ 8-plane and PMAGB-EA as a *Factory* *Installed*
PXG+ 24-plane graphics accelerator.

On page 1.22 it says "Field-installable PXG+ ... graphics options do not
include DEC Open3D license; must be ordered separately."   It then goes
on to list order numbers for both VMS/AXP and OSF/1 versions of this
software.

Clearly, you could buy a 3000/300 (the 500 & 600 are also listed
with similar configurations) system with the PGX+ factory installed,
running either VMS and OSF/1.

This seems to contradict all the assertions that DEC made people
aware of any lack of support.   There is nothing in this Systems
and Options Catalog that even implies a future withdrawal of
support for the PXG and/or PXG+.   On the contrary, a reasonable
person who reads this catalog would assume that they are a
standard configuration.

