OS/2 uses the NFS_USER (or something like that) uid set in config.sys when 
it's doing the mounting. The DUnix machine must be set up with "allow non-root 
mounts" if you are not using uid=0 from the OS/2 machine. If you want to allow 
non-root mounts, run the nfssetup script again on the DUnix machine; this can 
be run during production (but I wouldn't recommend it).

good luck

/Marek



