Majordomo gets my vote.

Home page(s) are at:

http://www.greatcircle.com/majordomo/

Software is at:

ftp://ftp.greatcircle.com/pub/majordomo/majordomo-1.93,tar.Z

The only version of perl5 I've found that works with Majordomo on OSF is
5.001m, which you can get from ...

ftp://ftp.netlabs.com/pub/outgoing/perl5.0/perl5.001m.tar.gz

... if you don't alread have it.  Perl5 should compile out of the box by
accepting the default config (./configure -def, I think).

Make sure you read the Majordomo FAQ ...

http://www.greatcircle.com/majordomo/FAQ

... and the README in the distribution before starting the install.

If you decide to install Majordomo, it's probably worth joining the
majordomo-users mailing list for a while.  Send mail to
majordomo@greatcircle.com with ...

subscribe majordomo-users

... as the first and only line of your message.

Although the current version of Majordomo (1.93) has many faults, it is
solid enough once you get the hang of it.  A significant new release is
due out "real soon now"..

If you run "large" lists, with lots of different domains involved, you
might also want to consider bulk_mailer, which speeds up delivery but
chews up memory.  It's at:

ftp://cs.utk.edu/pub/moore/bulk_mailer/

