There are two ways to change this:

The easiest way is to get the netconfig utility from:

ftp://cs.ucsd.edu/pub/csl/Netconfig/netconfig2.3.tar.gz

The other way is to use dbx -k.  For example

dbx -k /vmunix
print  tcp_keepalive	; prints value
a tcp_keepalive=value	; Sets new value
			; no need to reboot
			; but not written to disk
patch tcp_keepalive=value	;  Writes out to disk permanently
quit

Greg

BTW.... Does anyone know the correct kernel variable that controls
the amount of time that the kernel keeps TCP connections in TIME_WAIT?



