I'm not familiar with hylafax, but COSI puts out some very nice, 
inexpensive, easily-integrated fax software. They hide out at 
http://www.cosi.com/ ... I've been using their TruFax for a number of 
years (they've updated and renamed it now) and it's very solid. Their 
package is a collection of (mostly command-line) utilities, including a 
laser printer emulator, nice X-based viewer, virtual enlarging and 
reducing photocopier, file converter, etc., plus the usual daemon. This 
design doesn't make for a convenient joe-user level interface out of the 
box, but it's perfect for integrating into other applications. They use 
some interesting concepts, such as a "sheaf" of pages (a text file 
listing all of the component files that make up a document), multiple 
bins for the laser printer emulator (you can place "letterhead" or a 
"form" into one of the bins, and the emulator will merge images), etc.

Hope this is useful.

Chris Tyler  <CTyler@Oxford.NET>
Global Proximity Corporation





