In article <31180919.43A7@meritsl.co.uk> Rob Gray <robert.gray@meritsl.co.uk> writes:
#I have an Alpha 8200 running Dec Unix V3.2c, NSR V3.1a (BRX311) and 
#Media changer software V3.0 (CLC300)
#
#I would like to be able to use Networker SingleServer to run a 80Gb
#backup to a TZ877 (7 tape stacker), automatically using consecutive
#tapes within the stacker.

NetWorker SingleServer will not work with jukeboxes, that is a specific
limitation of the product.  You will have to upgrade to a full server
to use the TL877 as a jukebox.  You are currently describing using
NetWorker with a loader, so the instructions for setting up NetWorker
with a loader is what you need to look at.  When you install the
license PAK for the full server and a tier-1 jukebox license PAK, you
will be able to configure NetWorker to use the TL877 as a jukebox.
Since you mention having the full license below, you should be able 
to use the TL877 as a loader until the jukebox license arrives.
(Note that using a loader without a license is subject to change in
future releases).

#I am able to do smaller backups to a tape using rmt0h as long as the
#tape is loaded manually using the tape drive control buttons.

Hmmm, if you only use rmt0h, it won't work properly with NSR.  You
will need to use the non rewinding device (nrmt0h) or you will overwrite
the label written to the media.

#I have loaded the NAS200 license and NAS v7.0 (n20700) which includes
#the NSR server license. I am aware that an additional license is 
#required (jukebox tier 1) and is on the way. Will the lack of this
#license stop the jukebox being seen or will it just stop it being 
#used?

If you have this loaded, you are not running SingleServer.  Unless
you haven't shut NSR down and restarted nsrd after you've loaded/reset
the proper licenses into LMF.  Check in the upper corner of the nwadmin
GUI to find out what you are running.  Not having the jukebox license
will stop you from using the jukebox from NSR.  

#As an aside, I cannot find the manual for Networker on the 
#documentation CD of October 1995. Is it missing or am I just going
#blind?

The postscript documentation for NetWorker should be shipped with
the product, there have never been bookreader versions of the
documentation.  In the BRX311 kit you need to install the BRXRNOTES311
subset and look in /usr/kits/BRX311/doc directory.  The Admin_guide.ps
and Addendum.ps are of particular interest.  They can take some time
to print out, so be prepared.  I think a lot of problems will clear up
for you, once you have the documentation.

regards,

Amy Lenox
lenox@zso.dec.com
all standard disclaimers apply



