To check the number max number of user and system processes
look in the kernel configuration file -- /usr/sys/conf/<machinename>

The entries of interest are

maxproc   (default I believe is 130)

to increase this, add entry

maxproc 300     (or whatever you need)

This is the maximum processes allowed in a system

another is

maxuprc

The maximum number of processes that any one user can have
It is not a good idea to make maxproc and maxuprc the same, but
instead make maxuprc less that maxproc.  This avoids the problem
where too many processses from a user and the root not being able
to login and kill rude user processes.   

I hope this helps.



