	Just to clarify this issue, DEC announced when it introduced
the first alpha systems that the PXG and PXG+ boards would not have
continued support.  DEC provided such support to help PXG users, and
I'm one of them, through three major releases of the operating system.
In version 4, the support goes away.

	DEC has been telling the PXG users for a LONG time that the
boards would not have continued support.  I am sorry that it comes as
a surprise to some users, but it is not a change of direction by DEC.
They have been very consistent on this issue.

	As an aside, those PXG boards are significantly slower than
any of the replacement boards offered by DEC.  Video products have
improved significantly since the days of PXG+ turbo boards.

	All the best,

	Peter David








