that's true but there are 2 problems:

* it has (maybe had) a security hole if you chmod it root u+s (see
  comp.os.linux.announce - security)

* it has problems with utmp (or was it wtmp ?) - open an rxvt, call "login"
  there, log in and then logout and now do a "w" - you'll see that your entry
  is still there until someone else takes your pty - this sort of things often
  confuses OSF^H^H^HDigital UNIX's wall or shutdown

but i think you should be ok if you don't use the utmp (or was it wtmp ?)
support (and thus don't do an root chmod u+s)

