> The machine receives and displays text with accented characters with
> no obvious problems.  However, if I forward such text in mail, the
> accents are stripped.

The native OSF sendmail (aka King James sendmail) is not 8-bit clean.
Install sendmail V8 (this fixes also some security holes).

> In addition, I have not figured out how to enter accented text from
> the keyset.

This depends on your keyboard.  If you have a normal qwerty keyboard
(like most programmers seem to have), select one key which you don't
normally use and make that the mode-switch key with xmodmap.  I use
Caps Lock for that.  My .xmodmaprc looks like that:
  remove Lock = Caps_Lock
  keycode 66 = Mode_switch
  add mod2 = Mode_switch
(You will have different keycodes.  Check with xev.)
Now you can define key combinations for accented characters, for example
  keycode 34 = bracketleft braceleft adiaeresis Adiaeresis
  keycode 35 = bracketright braceright odiaeresis Odiaeresis
  keycode 51 = backslash bar udiaeresis Udiaeresis
  keycode 20 = minus underscore ssharp ssharp



