As Rob Hooft wrote in a followup, it appeared that there were some source
changes made (perhaps to fix latent program bugs) and now his application
runs faster using the most recent compiler.

DEC Fortran and DEC Fortran 90 are certainly compatible with Digital UNIX
3.2c.  If you are having problems with either compiler, please let us know!
Don't just wait and see if things sort themselves out!

In many cases, programs which fail at higher optimization levels have
errors in their programming which are revealed by optimization.  (And yes,
the compilers do sometimes have bugs as well.)  But we believe that the
default -O4 optimization is highly reliable.

If you are having problems, please send us an example.  If you have a support
contract, you can contact your local Digital support organization - this is
the way you could get fixes fastest.   However, I would encourage you to
send the example to fortran@digital.com (that goes to me) as well so we can
look at it and tell you what we find.  We are not mind-readers.  If you
are having a problem with our compilers, please tell us!  It is our #1 
priority to fix compiler bugs.
