In article <311A1F42.41C6@mccabe.com>, Aaron <aaron@mccabe.com> writes:
>im getting the message
> fork/procdup: task_create failed. Code: 0x11
>
>in the console. and am having trouble starting new shells
>all of a sudden.  what is this?  is it different from 
>task table full?  how do i fix it?

You've hit the per-uid process limit -- maxuprc. You can up this
by adding this line to /etc/sysconfigtab:

proc:
	max-proc-per-user = 64

and rebooting.

This is the same as changing the value of maxuprc in the config
file and rebuilding/rebooting the kernel.

-- 

