The serial number is way too big. It is defined as a 32-bit unsigned integer
which limits its value to 4,294,967,295. You need to revise the serial number
ot a smaller value.

Also, for any normal system a 5 minute refresh is a bit extreme. Typical values
are in small number of hours for both refresh and retry. The 1 minute retry
could be especially ill advised if there are several zones from a single
primary and that primary goes down. 14400 for refresh and 7200 or 14400 for
retry should be quite reasonable.

