Tommy Lindberg wrote:
> if the object file format on DEC's OSF/1 for alpha changed so much between V2.0
> and V3.2 that V2.0 can't link edit objects from V3.2?
> 
> Thank you in advance.
> 
> Tommy

In V3.2 we added a new section, .rconst.  The V2.0 linker doesn't 
understand the new section.  In general, it's not supported to move
objects back to older releases.  It is supported to move old objects
to newer releases.

