In article <4em1th$eo8@jethro.Corp.Sun.COM>, evelyn@rubyl.corp.sun.com (Evelyn Zhan) writes:

>I am trying to collect hard disk informations, such as disk label, disk
>capacity, SCSI id, etc, on OSF1 and ULTRIX. But I don't know how.  I don't
>have the root access, and I need the info as an output of a command in ascci
>format.

The SCSI ID is encoded in the minor device number.  The details are
in the SCSI manual page.  The partition table, label, geometry and
general device information all require read access to the device.
The ways of getting the information all require read access to
devices that are typically read protected...

Partition table:

	ULTRIX       - chpt(8), requires read access to device
	Digital UNIX - disklabel(8), requires read access to device

Capacity and Geometry

	ULTRIX	     - DEVGETGEOM I/O control, requires read access device
	Digital UNIX - DEVGETGEOM I/O control, ditto
	Both         - scu(8), requires read access to /dev/cam.

General information:

	Both - DEVIOCGET I/O control, requires read access to device.

It seems pretty clear that you can't get there from here without
a program running as root or changing the permissions of devices
so that you can read them.  The middle ground is write a program
that does these operations and can run setuid root to give read
access so these I/O controls will work.  

