This only  postponed another grinding halt. vmstat -M shows lots of CRED and
KALLOC (20Mb and 12 Mb resp. on my system when it finally died). It looks like
a kernel/daemon memory leak associated with authorisation, and aggravated by
NFS V3, which we use as we have an OSF file-server. A patch is being developed
by Digital - it's not in V3.2d. A workaround is to use NFS V2 (mount -o nfsv2).

